IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-80, TARGETED: the Defamation (Prohibition) Law, 5725-1965 ("the Law"). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two items, I1 and I2, as typed values and tests them.
-- I1: the words of paragraph (6) of section 13 name an Ordinance that section 30 of a later law prints with the word בטלה.
-- I2: the words of section 7 name section numbers of the Ordinance of 1944, and the comparison table of the New Version of that Ordinance prints rows for them.
-- SEAT: the person who sues, or is sued, over a publication to which section 7, section 13 or section 15 of the Law is applied. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument, a printed text, a named instrument, a footnote, an instruction on words, a commencement as the page prints it, a row of the comparison table, an item, and the questions asked of them.
-- No reference is stated here; they are in df80-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A date typed as an issue date is the date the footer of the issue prints; it is NOT a commencement date.
-- A commencement is typed separately, and only where a page prints one; where a page prints none the value is NOTHING.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A way a fact was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `not checked`

DECLARE `A kind of instruction` IS ONE OF
    `Delete words`
    `Insert words`

-- An instrument as the row cites it. The issue date is the one a footer prints; the New Version's footers print none, so its issue date is NOTHING.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its citation in the row` IS A STRING
    `its issue date` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- A text as an instrument printed it: a section, a paragraph, a title or a footnote line.
DECLARE `A printed text` HAS
    `the instrument that printed it` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A name that a paragraph uses for another instrument, and how far the row read that instrument.
DECLARE `A named instrument` HAS
    `the words that name it` IS A STRING
    `how the row read it` IS A `A way a fact was read`

-- An instruction an instrument prints about words of the Law. The words are copied from the ext: line above the value.
DECLARE `An instruction on words` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page it is on` IS A NUMBER
    `the item` IS A NUMBER
    `the kind` IS A `A kind of instruction`
    `the section of the Law it names` IS A NUMBER
    `the paragraphs it names` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `the words it names` IS A STRING
    `the words it comes after` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- A commencement as the page prints it. The date is typed only where a page prints a calendar date.
DECLARE `A commencement as read` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the date the page prints` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `how it was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`

-- A row of the comparison table of the New Version. Cells are typed in reading order (right to left), as the crop shows them.
-- `its place among the rows of its band` counts the rows of one printed band from the top, starting at 1.
DECLARE `A row of the comparison table` HAS
    `the old-section cell` IS A STRING
    `the old section number` IS A NUMBER
    `the old section letter` IS A STRING
    `the new-section cell` IS A STRING
    `its place among the rows of its band` IS A NUMBER

-- An item of the row, with its two limbs.
DECLARE `An item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `A way a fact was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

GIVEN t IS A `A printed text`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed text contains the words` MEANS CONTAINS (t's `its words`) w

GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the first instrument was issued after the second` MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `its issue date`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST da THEN
        CONSIDER b's `its issue date`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST db THEN da > db

-- I1: the name is printed together with the word בטלה in one of the texts in the list.
GIVEN name IS A STRING, ts IS A LIST OF `A printed text`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the name is printed with the word בטלה in a text in the list` MEANS
    any (GIVEN t YIELD (CONTAINS (t's `its words`) name) AND (CONTAINS (t's `its words`) "בטלה")) ts

-- A set of printed texts, as a record so that a function can take it before a list.
DECLARE `A set of printed texts` HAS
    `the texts` IS A LIST OF `A printed text`

-- I1, the red question: no named instrument that the row read is printed with בטלה in a text of the set.
-- An instrument typed `not checked` is outside the question.
GIVEN tx IS A `A set of printed texts`, ns IS A LIST OF `A named instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no named instrument that the row read is printed with בטלה in a text of the set` MEANS
    all (GIVEN n YIELD (n's `how the row read it` EQUALS `not checked`) OR (NOT (`the name is printed with the word בטלה in a text in the list` (n's `the words that name it`) (tx's `the texts`)))) ns

-- I2: positional questions about the bands of the table. A list is always the last parameter.
GIVEN above IS A `A row of the comparison table`, below IS A `A row of the comparison table`, rows IS A LIST OF `A row of the comparison table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A row of the comparison table`
`the rows printed between two rows` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD ((r's `its place among the rows of its band`) > (above's `its place among the rows of its band`)) AND ((r's `its place among the rows of its band`) < (below's `its place among the rows of its band`))) rows

GIVEN above IS A `A row of the comparison table`, below IS A `A row of the comparison table`, cell IS A STRING, rows IS A LIST OF `A row of the comparison table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a row whose old-section cell is the cell is printed between two rows` MEANS
    any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the old-section cell` EQUALS cell) (`the rows printed between two rows` above below rows)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, letter IS A STRING, words IS A STRING, rows IS A LIST OF `A row of the comparison table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some row for the old section prints the words in its new-section cell` MEANS
    any (GIVEN r YIELD CONTAINS (r's `the new-section cell`) words)
        (filter (GIVEN r YIELD ((r's `the old section number`) EQUALS n) AND ((r's `the old section letter`) EQUALS letter)) rows)

GIVEN letter IS A STRING, rows IS A LIST OF `A row of the comparison table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some row prints the letter after its old section number` MEANS
    any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the old section letter` EQUALS letter) rows

GIVEN words IS A STRING, rows IS A LIST OF `A row of the comparison table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some old-section cell contains the words` MEANS
    any (GIVEN r YIELD CONTAINS (r's `the old-section cell`) words) rows

GIVEN c IS AN `An item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`
